; Unicode identifier tables for the TypeScript lexer.
;
; A code point above ASCII is only an identifier character when Unicode says
; so; treating every such code point as a letter accepted programs like
; `var 🀒` and rejected nothing. The ID_Start / ID_Continue sets are
; stored as delta-encoded ranges (base 36, "gap.length" pairs separated by
; commas) and decoded once per lexer into a flat [lo, hi, lo, hi, ...] table.

